h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 872)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Reopen works on an ended review.</b> The Review Manager&#8217;s Reopen on a row that has ended brings the session back and hosts it again as a new review under the same name and passphrase, with the Share window open &#8212; make a new web link if you need one.</li>
<li><b>The review name defaults to yours</b> &#8212; &#8220;James Rogers&#8217;s Review&#8221; &#8212; and Join a Review&#8217;s review menu is always there, saying so while it looks.</li>
<li><b>Web review: the gamma menu moves the whole picture again.</b> Auto corrects the video&#8217;s browser lift alone (so playing and pausing still match); Darken and Lighten are your display intent and go on the still and the canvases too.</li>
<li>The Network window fills its frame &#8212; the picker&#8217;s last segment no longer clips in a narrow window, and the content no longer floats off-centre in a wide one.</li>
<li>A long passphrase shrinks to fit its capsule instead of losing its middle.</li>
<li>The invite sheet is as wide as its content &#8212; a fixed width clipped the heading and the notes on both sides.</li>
<li>Two copies of Asobi on one Mac can both host nearby: when the usual port is taken the second opens its door on a free one instead of failing with &#8220;Address already in use&#8221;.</li>
<li>The share history is safe with two copies of Asobi running on one Mac.</li>
<li>Manual: the review windows pictured (Share This Review, Join a Review, the invite sheet, Network); the slow-connection warning and where a host sees it; Reopen on an ended review; the web gamma menu.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
